<strings>
    <string id="AppName">Carb Burn</string>
    <!-- Display name of the beta build variant (manifest.beta.xml). One
         resources/ tree serves both manifests, so this string ships in the
         PRODUCTION build too, where nothing references it.

         It costs +32 bytes per production .prg - measured, not estimated: the
         release build was repeated with this string removed, and every one of
         the 13 devices came out exactly 32 bytes smaller (edge840
         14908 -> 14940, fenix7 13084 -> 13116, edge1050 25036 -> 25068, 13/13
         at +32). Judged worth paying to keep one strings file; if the
         data-field memory budget ever gets tight, this is 32 bytes to reclaim.

         CONSEQUENCE, and the reason this note matters: the literal
         "Carb Burn (Beta)" is present in the production .prg as well (offset
         12985 on edge840). The app-name string is therefore NOT usable as
         evidence of which manifest a build consumed. Only the embedded 16-byte
         application id discriminates - which is what the CI guards check. -->
    <string id="AppNameBeta">Carb Burn (Beta)</string>
    <string id="FtpTitle">FTP (watts)</string>
    <string id="Lt1Title">LT1 / aerobic threshold (watts, 0 = not tested)</string>
    <string id="GeTitle">Gross efficiency (%)</string>
    <string id="WeightTitle">Body weight (kg, match Garmin profile)</string>
    <string id="IntakeTitle">Carb intake during ride (g/h)</string>
</strings>
